uns 75 years, from 1951 to 2025, and on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 6 grids November to December came in under 90% of normal in 40 of them. In 2025, July to August finished at 50% of normal and August to September at 49% on the middle of the grids. So far in 2026, March to April sits at 167% of normal and April to May at 159% on the middle of the grids. Grid 21446 had its driest year in 1980, at 55% of normal.</p>"}
